meta {
  name: 1.Get Report Templates
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/report/templates
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Step 1 of the Reports flow — lists all available report templates (Reports API, the "flatter" CSV
  export covering up to 13 months of history) and their numeric `Id` values.

  **Parameters**: none — returns every template available to your org.

  **Usage**: Find the template you want (e.g. "Calling Detailed Call History") and note its `Id`
  (e.g. `500`) and `maxDays`, then use it to populate the body of "2.Create Report".

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/report-templates/list-report-templates

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
